# FSD Architecture Rules

## Layer Import Direction (strictly downward)
pages → widgets → features → entities → shared-app

## File Placement
- Pages: `src/pages/<PageName>.tsx`
- Widget UI: `src/widgets/<pageName>/ui/<PageName>.tsx` — pure presentational, NO logic, NO types
- Widget Model: `src/widgets/<pageName>/models/use<PageName>Model.ts`
- Widget Types: `src/widgets/<pageName>/types/index.ts`
- Feature UI: `src/features/<featureName>/ui/<FeatureName>.tsx`
- Feature API: `src/features/<featureName>/api/<featureName>Api.ts`
- Feature Model: `src/features/<featureName>/models/use<FeatureName>.ts`
- Entity UI: `src/entities/<entityName>/ui/<EntityName>.tsx`
- Entity API: `src/entities/<entityName>/api/<entityName>Api.ts`
- Shared: `src/shared-app/<componentName>/`

## Hard Rules
- UI files: zero logic, zero useState/useEffect, zero type definitions, zero API calls
- Types: always in `types/index.ts` — never define inline in UI
- API calls: only in `api/<name>Api.ts` — never in UI or models
- Cross-layer imports are forbidden (e.g. feature importing from widget)
- One root composer UI file per slice (`ui/<SliceName>.tsx`) + sub-components in the same `ui/` folder
- Allowed sub-folders only: `ui/`, `models/`, `types/`, `api/`, `store/`, `logics/`

## Naming
- Widget/Feature/Entity folders: camelCase
- UI component files: PascalCase.tsx
- Model files: `use<Name>Model.ts` or `use<Name>.ts`
- API files: `<name>Api.ts`
- Store files: `<name>Store.ts`
- Types file: always `index.ts`
